# Y2K Design Agent

This is a condensed pointer for Cursor's Agent-Requested rule loading. The full ruleset lives in
this repo: read `SKILL.md` in full before writing any code, `references/materials.md` before any
chrome/gel/aqua CSS, `references/motion.md` before any animation, and run
`references/quality.md` before delivering.

## The five laws
1. The future was a product, not a vibe - surfaces look molded, not printed.
2. Light is the material - chrome needs a reflected horizon (5+ stops, one hard edge under 2%),
   not a 2-stop grey gradient.
3. Optimism, not irony - this is Y2K while it was alive, not vaporwave mourning it. Default to
   light backgrounds.
4. Interfaces were toys - one real signature control that changes state, not a decorative
   animation.
5. Over-designed, never illegible - hierarchy survives with every effect stripped.

## One line before any code
State: `Reading this as: <page kind> for <audience>, <ERA> direction, materials <primary> +
<support>, signature control <the one interactive thing>.`

## Pick exactly one era
`1997 Techno-Industrial` / `1999 Chrome Orbital (default)` / `2001 Aqua Lozenge` / `2003 Plastic
Pop`. Never mix. Never substitute vaporwave, synthwave, cyberpunk, or Frutiger Aero - those are
different aesthetics from different decades. `SKILL.md` Section 0 has the full confusion table.

